.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-INVITE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-invite - Invite a member by email, including before signup


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team invite <team> <email> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Invite a person by email address. They do not need an account yet: they sign in, verify
that email address, then accept the invitation. The invitation is for the member role and
expires; change the role afterwards with pb team role.

.PP
The team needs a spare seat, otherwise the invitation is refused and you must add seats first.
Pass the team's current generation with --generation (read it with pb team get). A stale
generation is rejected, so two people editing the team never overwrite each other.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--generation\fP=0
	expected current team generation

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for invite

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb team get acme
  pb team invite acme ana@example.test --generation 7
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team(1)\fP
